                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Great strategic game play for god-wannabes. Setting up your god-avatar has lots of variability and great choices (from a stationary magic fountain, to some color of dragon, to mythical creatures like a manticore or cyclops--each faction has a selection of god-chassis).  Like Greek gods? Be one. Or start as a powerful human wizard or druid.\n\nFaction troops are fantasy variants of historical cultures, but massively twisted in creatively magical ways (Roman lizard-riders?). Over twenty factions, each with an \"early\", \"middle\" and \"late\" variation. Troops must be assigned to \"leader\" units before they can be used aggressively. \n\nMagic economy is via seven different colors of magic gems, each representing a specialized type of magic  (faux-Incans raid for blood slaves in addition). Site-searching for gems, income, and special places is critical. Magic resources are allocated between \"tactical\" spells (by giving gems to spell-casting leaders) and campaign-changing \"global\" spells cast at a laboratory site. \n\nStationary militias can be established to protect your holdings. Once bought, these will regenerate as long as you hold their province. \n\nScouts/spies are available--important to know what you're up against. Some factions have assassins as well. Reliable mercenary bands, as well as wizards and a super-assassin can be hired, if you win the bid. \n\nPaint the whole map your religion, slay or dominion-snuff your opponents, and ascend. \n\nStrategic movement is a little clunky, but is essentially order assignment to leaders. \n\nTurn-end resolution occurs when all orders are in. A results report at the beginning of your next turn allows review of your tactical battles, which run automatically according to your pre-assigned scripting.\n\nRetro pixel graphics may not be to everyone's taste. Your tactical control is limited to pre-scripts, so your tactical troop placements and spell assignments are important.\n\nThis is an exceptional 4x game that multi-plays very differently than solo. In solo there are AI habits you can learn to simplify your life. In multiplayer, the scope for achieving strategic surprise is huge.  It's never been off my rig since I bought it.\n\nActually, there's only one bogus thing in this game--and it's awesome! \n[\"no spoiler\" alert = not spoiling it!]",
